# The druids' people who gave up after a fight at the Wizard of Wines or on Yester Hill (F13, story/captives.gd).

~ start
Narrator: The last of the druids' people sits down hard in the dirt, spent, chest heaving. Mud and berry juice streak the paint on his face.
-> choose

~ choose
* [Intimidation DC 13] Ask what the druids want with the winery. -> hill | mute
* [Persuasion DC 13] Ask what they are building on the hill. -> hill | shrug
* [if at:wizard_of_wines or at:wizard_of_wines_winery or at:wizard_of_wines_press_house or at:wizard_of_wines_cellar] Leave them to the Martikovs. -> hand_over
* Let them go. -> release
* Kill them. -> kill

~ hill
Narrator: 'A body for the lord in the castle,' he says, 'a giant of earth and thorn on Yester Hill. It needs a heart. The stone from your vintner's vines is that heart. When the chant is finished, it walks.'
-> after_talk

~ mute
Narrator: He starts to hum, low and tuneless, and won't stop. It sounds like wind in dry branches.
-> after_talk

~ shrug
Narrator: 'You'll see it,' he says, almost kindly. 'Everyone in the valley will see it.'
-> after_talk

~ after_talk
* [if at:wizard_of_wines or at:wizard_of_wines_winery or at:wizard_of_wines_press_house or at:wizard_of_wines_cellar] Leave them to the Martikovs. -> hand_over
* Let them go. -> release
* Kill them. -> kill

~ hand_over
Narrator: The Martikovs bind them with vine-cord and lock them in an empty vat to wait for a cart to Vallaki. The ravens on the press-house roof watch with interest.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +2 kip_smudgewick +1: You left the druids' people to the Martikovs' judgement
-> END

~ release
Narrator: He goes, limping, toward the hills. Whether he goes home or back to the chant, you can't tell.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 wren_featherfoot +2 thistle +1: You let the druids' beaten people go
-> END

~ kill
Narrator: The crows come down before you have even cleaned your blade.
approve godrick_pendlebrook -5 liriel_dawnsong -4 wren_featherfoot -4 thistle -2 kip_smudgewick -1: You killed the druids' people after they gave up
-> END
